&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="line-height: 1.6em; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 200; color: #fafafa;"&gt;🚀 &lt;strong&gt;Frontend&lt;/strong&gt; Focus&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;div style="color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;#​760 — September 30, 2026 | &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191061/rss" style="color: #fafafa;  font-weight: 600;"&gt;Read on the web&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191016/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/wqdeehcjo7y0imo6gazv.jpg" width="640" style="      line-height: 100%;  "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191016/rss" title="github.blog" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.25em; font-weight: 400;"&gt;Improving Site Performance by Shipping More CSS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — GitHub details how it spent three years purging &lt;code&gt;styled-components&lt;/code&gt; and 'CSS-in-JS' from &lt;code&gt;github․com&lt;/code&gt; in favor of CSS Modules. The result? Shipping &lt;em&gt;more&lt;/em&gt; CSS, but GitHub reports 55% less time to server-side render a page.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Josh Black and Marie Lucca (GitHub) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;💡 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191017/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;CSS Modules&lt;/a&gt; isn't a browser feature or standard, but a &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191018/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;widely supported&lt;/a&gt; bundler convention where classes in a &lt;code&gt;.module.css&lt;/code&gt; file get rewritten to unique names, scoping styles per file with no runtime cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191015/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/a1e7f4cb.png" width="110" height="110" style="padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px;     line-height: 100%; "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191015/rss" title="www.tigerdata.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Reports That Time Out Aren't a Frontend Bug&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — The report worked in testing. In production, it scans months of rows and times out before it renders. That's not a frontend bug, it's the query behind it. TimescaleDB extends Postgres so that query returns fast at scale. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191015/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Get $1000 credit to start&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tiger Data (creators of TimescaleDB) &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191019/rss" title="emdashcms.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;EmDash 1.0: An Open Source CMS for Astro&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Cloudflare's alternative to WordPress, first announced in April, has reached 1.0. Each site ships with an MCP server, meaning you can set an agent to work out of the box. To accompany the launch, &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191020/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;plugins can now be submitted&lt;/a&gt; to &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191021/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;its registry&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Matt Kane &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191022/rss" title="claude.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;How Anthropic Made Claude's Web App Faster&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — The tale of how a recent sprint (with Claude doing much of the work) cut Claude's time-to-typeable at the 75th percentile from 3.1s to 0.55s, from tracking layout shifts too small for CLS to flag, to a &lt;code&gt;:root:has()&lt;/code&gt; selector costing 24ms per DOM change, and a jump caused by Chrome pre-rendering the page at the wrong height.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wang, Attard, and G (Anthropic) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;"&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;⚡️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;IN BRIEF&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌀 Cloudflare has &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191023/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;launched Turnstile Spin&lt;/a&gt;, a way to let AI agents set up Turnstile's protection on sites you're building. Cloudflare now also has &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191024/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;a new &lt;code&gt;cf&lt;/code&gt; CLI client&lt;/a&gt; which can work with all of its APIs (unlike Wrangler).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧭 Safari Technology Preview 253 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191025/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;is out now&lt;/a&gt;, adding support for network throttling within the Web Inspector, amongst a huge number of fixes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🦊 Firefox 157 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191026/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;has a new look&lt;/a&gt;, which you can &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191027/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;see in action here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📉 In response to recent &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191028/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;chatter around the 'death' of web education&lt;/a&gt;, Andy Bell shares &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191029/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;a bleak sketch&lt;/a&gt; of where things stand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🟢 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191030/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Version 31 of developer browser Polypane is out now&lt;/a&gt;, adding a new canvas layout, elements panel improvements, and an update to Chromium 155.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔥 Got something you want to say about HTML? Manuel Matuzović is &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191031/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;seeking submissions for this year's HTMHell Advent Calendar&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;📙&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;"&gt;Articles, Opinions &amp;amp; Tutorials&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191032/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1790768407/sqfroq51wfjasopm9vyc.png" width="640" style="    line-height: 100%;      "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191032/rss" title="ishadeed.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Detect When Elements Overlap with CSS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A neat bit of CSS lateral thinking to detect when two elements get too close or overlap, no JavaScript needed. It combines anchor positioning, style container queries, and scroll-driven animations, using an overflowing 'measure' element as the trigger.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ahmad Shadeed &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191033/rss" title="developer.chrome.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Connection Allowlists: Lock Down Where a Page Can Connect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Chrome 152 adds support for a &lt;code&gt;Connection-Allowlist&lt;/code&gt; header to tell the browser which servers a page is allowed to talk to (and block everything else).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Benz &amp;amp; Zapata (Chrome for Developers) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191034/rss" title="master.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The Future of Frontend Is Agentic: Free OpenAI Course&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Join OpenAI's Katia Gil Guzman and learn how to direct Codex through landing pages, dashboards, 3D interfaces, and shipping into an existing codebase.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Master.dev &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191035/rss" title="olliewilliams.xyz" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Which Features Should Browsers Fix Together in 2027?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Ollie shares what features he believes the web platform should focus on next year, including the &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191036/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Sanitizer API&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191037/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;code&gt;focusgroup&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191038/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;code&gt;grid-lanes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, along with what early-stage things should be in consideration for the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ollie Williams &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191039/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1790770351/syci9fg7mqolp1gcvoci.png" width="640" style="    line-height: 100%;      "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191039/rss" title="blog.master.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Extracting Grid Information Using CSS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A neat CSS-only proof of concept technique where you can get information about a grid structure (number of columns/rows, where items sit on the grid, etc). The technique relies on scroll-driven animations, oddly enough.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Temani Afif &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191040/rss" title="interfaces.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The Interface Cheat Sheet&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A helpful illustrated list of good UI advice, touching on points from border radiuses and transitions to the use of color, scaling and accessibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jakub Krehel &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191041/rss" title="try.expo.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The Era of Agentic Mobile Development Is Built on Expo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Build with our CLI and dev tools. Test on our cloud simulators. And ship with the best CI/CD for mobile development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Expo &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191042/rss" title="www.keithcirkel.co.uk" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Custom Attributes Polyfill&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A polyfill for the proposed Custom Attributes spec, letting you attach reusable behaviours to any element via custom attributes with their own lifecycle hooks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Keith Cirkel &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191043/rss" title="blog.damato.design" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Fluid Typography&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Donnie argues that because container widths are unpredictable, using container queries to drive fluid font sizing isn't the right choice. He suggests we stick with viewport units to retain true control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Donnie D’Amato &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191044/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;"&gt;Stop Buttons Triggering Zoom When They’re Double Tapped&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;"&gt;Andy Bell&lt;/span&gt; 
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191045/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;"&gt;Stop Treating CSS Container Queries Like Traditional Media Queries&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;"&gt;Victor Ayomipo&lt;/span&gt; 
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191046/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;"&gt;Component Testing: A Practical Guide for Frontend Developers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;"&gt;Storybook Blog&lt;/span&gt; 
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
