&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="line-height: 1.6em; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 200; color: #fafafa;"&gt;🚀 &lt;strong&gt;Frontend&lt;/strong&gt; Focus&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;div style="color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;#​759 — September 23, 2026 | &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190756/rss" style="color: #fafafa;  font-weight: 600;"&gt;Read on the web&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190725/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/urmdbbhgpgphno40bksv.jpg" width="640" style="      line-height: 100%;  "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;🧭&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190725/rss" title="webkit.org" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.25em; font-weight: 400;"&gt;WebKit Features for Safari 27.0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — An &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190726/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;epic set of release notes&lt;/a&gt; covers Safari 27's enhancements, including &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190727/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;its new MCP server&lt;/a&gt; (let agents debug your work), &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190728/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;scroll anchoring&lt;/a&gt;, the customizable &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;select&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; element, a &lt;code&gt;controls&lt;/code&gt; attribute for images in visionOS, &lt;code&gt;sizes="auto"&lt;/code&gt; for images, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WebKit &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;💡 In related news, &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190729/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Xcode 27.1 Beta&lt;/a&gt; includes an &lt;em&gt;iPhone Duo&lt;/em&gt; simulator if you want to see how things look on Apple's forthcoming foldable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190724/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/338febeb.png" width="110" height="110" style="padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px;     line-height: 100%; "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190724/rss" title="www.tigerdata.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Skeleton Loaders Are Just Slow Queries in Disguise&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — You add a skeleton loader to hide the wait. But that wait is a slow query, and it only grows with your data. TimescaleDB extends Postgres so the data behind your components returns fast at scale, no matter how big it gets. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190724/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Get $1000 credit to start&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tiger Data (creators of TimescaleDB) &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190730/rss" title="flaviocopes.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;12 CSS Features You Can Use Today with No Build Step&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Highlights various CSS features that we can turn to &lt;em&gt;now&lt;/em&gt;, retiring some toolchain dependencies in turn. Things like native nesting instead of Sass, &lt;code&gt;:has()&lt;/code&gt; instead of wrapper-class hacks, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flavio Copes &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190731/rss" title="patrickbrosset.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Blurry Before Beautiful: Image Previews for the Web?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Having a 'blurry' version of an image load in before the full version isn't new, but the Edge team is proposing a &lt;code&gt;previewsrc&lt;/code&gt; attribute so browsers can handle it natively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Patrick Brosset (Microsoft) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;"&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;⚡️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;IN BRIEF&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🛠️ &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190732/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Chrome's latest DevTools update&lt;/a&gt; brings DevTools MCP server improvements, ad script tracking, more modern devices in Device Mode, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌏 A &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190733/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;recent Edge update&lt;/a&gt; adds the &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190734/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;OpaqueRange API&lt;/a&gt; for text-range UIs, component accessibility improvements, and the agent-ready WebMCP API.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;☑️ &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190735/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Chrome 155 beta adds support&lt;/a&gt; for the CSS &lt;code&gt;symbols()&lt;/code&gt; function, &lt;code&gt;margin-trim&lt;/code&gt;, JPEG XL images, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;📙&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;"&gt;Articles, Opinions &amp;amp; Tutorials&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190736/rss" title="polypane.app" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The Root Scroller and How Not to Lose It&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — The ‘root scroller’ is the viewport’s scroll container and handles things like scroll restoration and collapsing mobile address bars. But common CSS patterns can hand scrolling to other elements and lose those features, as shown in this demo-packed explainer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kilian Valkhof &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190740/rss" title="www.zachleat.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;"AI, Make the Website Good"&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Zach argues that, no matter the tools, caring about the &lt;em&gt;quality&lt;/em&gt; of output matters more than ever. He amusingly illustrates this point by highlighting the front of house output of top AI companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zach Leatherman &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190738/rss" title="try.expo.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The Era of Agentic Mobile Development Is Built on Expo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Build with our CLI and dev tools. Test on our cloud simulators. And ship with the best CI/CD for mobile development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Expo &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190739/rss" title="noti.st" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;19½ Things You Didn't Know About Accessibility in HTML and CSS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A neat slide-driven writeup of a StripeCon Europe talk rounds up lesser-known accessibility details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manuel Matuzovic &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190737/rss" title="cydstumpel.nl" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;'CSS Scroll-Triggered Animations Are Here, And I Completely Missed Them'&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Scroll-&lt;em&gt;triggered&lt;/em&gt; animations shipped in Chrome back in February. Cyd catches us up on how they differ from regular and scroll-driven animations, and looks at the &lt;code&gt;timeline-trigger&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;animation-trigger&lt;/code&gt; properties specifically.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cyd Stumpel &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190741/rss" title="developer.chrome.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Responsive &lt;code&gt;iframes&lt;/code&gt; in Chrome 154&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Landed in Chrome, and in preview in Edge, responsively-sized iframes are now a thing. You can set an iframe to be the size of its content, set which dimension that size is derived from, and tweak dynamically. The only catch is the embedded document must opt in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sebastian Benz &amp;amp; Bramus van Damme &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190742/rss" title="piccalil.li" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;A Decent Custom Checkbox Pattern for Until &lt;code&gt;::checkmark&lt;/code&gt; is Ready&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Until &lt;code&gt;::checkmark&lt;/code&gt; reaches checkboxes, Andy lays a transparent native input over a custom box with an SVG tick.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Andy Bell &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190743/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;"&gt;We Found a Fix for 'Wobbly Spinners' in Safari&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — CSS’s &lt;code&gt;round()&lt;/code&gt; function came to the rescue here.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;"&gt;Cody Olsen&lt;/span&gt; 
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190744/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;"&gt;The Death of Web Development Education: Rescuing a Field From Disappearing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;"&gt;Mathias Schäfer&lt;/span&gt; 
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;🧰&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;"&gt;Tools, Code &amp;amp; Resources&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190745/rss" title="github.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Critical 9.0: Extract and Inline Critical Path CSS in HTML&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A total rewrite of the popular critical CSS inliner, used to improve first render and LCP. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190746/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Version 9&lt;/a&gt; picks between two engines: a fast, browser-free one for prerendered HTML and a Playwright-based one for SPAs. Plus MCP support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Addy Osmani and Ben Zörb &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;📊&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190747/rss" title="plotly.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Plotly.js 4: A Major Update for the Popular Charting Library&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — It adds ‘quiver’ plots for drawing vector fields (with many fantastic examples in the post), accepts any CSS Color 4 color string, and removes the use of Mapbox GL in favor of MapLibre.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chris Parmer &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190748/rss" title="surveyjs.io" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Build Forms That Fit Your Frontend—and Any Backend&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Create custom themes for your form UI or use style adapters for Bootstrap, MUI, and Shadcn/UI. Dedicated npm packages for React, Angular, and Vue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SurveyJS &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190749/rss" title="rohanadwankar.github.io" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Semfont: A Font That Reads What You Wrote&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A small library that auto-styles text word-by-word, scoring each word (by sentiment, salience, and more) and then applying color, weight, and slant. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190750/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Repo here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rohan Adwankar &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190751/rss" title="sli.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Slidev: Presentation Slides for Developers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Uses a Vue-based tech stack, providing a developer-focused set of tools for creating Markdown-based slides for tech talks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthony Fu &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;🧪&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="   font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;"&gt;...and finally&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
