&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190070/rss" title="blog.master.dev" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.25em; font-weight: 400;"&gt;New Things You Should Know About HTML in 2026&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — HTML moves a bit slower than CSS and JavaScript, but there's plenty of new features to keep up with. Chris runs through several, including the &lt;code&gt;geolocation&lt;/code&gt; element, HTML-in-Canvas, camera and mic management via &lt;code&gt;usermedia&lt;/code&gt;, and the &lt;code&gt;model&lt;/code&gt; element. A great way to catch up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chris Coyier &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190071/rss" title="lea.verou.me" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The Best Dark Mode Toggle is Probably… &lt;em&gt;None&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — We recently shared &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190072/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;some thoughts from Lea&lt;/a&gt; on controls for switching between light/dark modes. After weeks of debate, including &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190073/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;a rebuttal from Bramus&lt;/a&gt;, she returns to ask whether most sites need an always-visible toggle &lt;em&gt;at all&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lea Verou &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190069/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/47ffe836.png" width="110" height="110" style="padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px;     line-height: 100%; "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190069/rss" title="master.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Free Course: Build Ambitious Modern Interfaces Faster with OpenAI Codex&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Join Katia Gil Guzman for this free Codex course and learn how agentic coding has changed frontend development. You'll cover setup, prompting, feedback, skills, automations, deployment and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Master.dev &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190074/rss" title="vale.rocks" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Antiquated HTML Snippets and Artefacts&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A tour of various snippets of code that commonly appear in HTML, but which are largely byproducts of a bygone era and are no longer needed. Conditional comments, &lt;code&gt;X-UA-Compatible&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;cleartype&lt;/code&gt; directives all make an appearance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Declan Chidlow &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;🗳️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190075/rss" title="www.w3.org" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;W3C Opens Its 2026 Community Survey&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — The W3C has launched its 2026 community-wide survey to gather input from developers and stakeholders on the future direction of its operations and web standards work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;W3C &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;"&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;⚡️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;IN BRIEF&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎉 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190108/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;The team behind Tailwind CSS is joining Shopify&lt;/a&gt; but &lt;em&gt;"nothing changes with Tailwind CSS or any of our other open-source projects."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📑 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190076/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Interop 2027 proposals are open until September 23&lt;/a&gt; — you can nominate the cross-browser gaps that most need fixing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🗓️ As promised, Chrome has now &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190078/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;moved to a two-week release cycle&lt;/a&gt;, with Firefox, Edge and Brave following suit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🖼️ JPEG XL support will &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190079/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;be enabled by default in Firefox 158&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🕵️ Years ago, a developer noticed Chrome exempted Google's own sites from the setting that wipes site data on exit (Google fixed it). Now, he claims &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190080/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;it's happening again as of Chrome 152&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏛️ InfoQ reflects on &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190081/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;jQuery 1.0 turning 20 years old&lt;/a&gt; and why it remains heavily used across the Web.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
