&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190082/rss" title="blog.master.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Creating a Custom Scrollbar Component in 2026&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — How to approach building high-performance custom scrollbars, replacing heavy JavaScript arithmetic with modern CSS features and handling sizing and visibility entirely within the stylesheet. A clean, modern approach to a classic UI challenge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alexander Inkin &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190083/rss" title="kciter.so" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The Browser's Main Thread is Expensive&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A thorough look, complete with demos, at spending your main thread time well, including splitting, batching, prioritizing, and deferring tasks, then how to get work off it entirely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sunhyoup Lee &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190084/rss" title="www.tigerdata.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The Loading State Isn't the Frontend's Fault&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — It's the query behind it. TimescaleDB extends Postgres so it returns fast as data grows. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190084/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Get $1000 credit to start&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tiger Data (creators of TimescaleDB) &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190085/rss" title="utilitybend.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Wiring Up Components with Typed &lt;code&gt;attr()&lt;/code&gt; and Container Style Queries&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Shows how to feed HTML attributes into CSS properties (like grid column counts or spacing units), then let style queries pass that state down to child components with no JavaScript state or utility classes required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brecht De Ruyte &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190086/rss" title="portswigger.net" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;CSS: The Weapon Inside Your Inbox&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — How CSS can be weaponized against popular webmail providers to do things it shouldn't be able to, like defacing the UI, bypassing image proxies, and building a keylogger.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gareth Heyes &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190087/rss" title="dropbox.tech" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Testing Cookie Behavior Across Hundreds of Web Surfaces with an In-House Auditor&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — An interesting ‘big corp’ case study looking at tooling built to audit cookie behavior at scale across various web properties.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Yasmin McDowell and Lawrence Good (Dropbox) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

